  "num_turns": null,
  "final_message": "I fixed the bug in `add_tag` in `tag_util.py`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes.\n\n**The bug:** `add_tag(record, tag, tags=[])` used a list as its default value. Python creates that list once and reuses it on every call. So tags added in one call showed up in the next unrelated call that left out `tags`.\n\n**The fix:** the default is now `tags=None`, and the function creates a new empty list whenever `tags` is `None`. If you pass your own list, the function still adds to that same list rather than a copy. I checked this with a quick manual run. `remove_tag` and `test_public.py` are unchanged.\n\nDONE: Fixed add_tag's shared list default by using `tags=None` and creating a new list per call; a list you pass in is still used as given; public tests pass.",
