      "final_message": "I rewrote `semver_compare` in `solution.py`. Both public tests pass, and a few extra edge-case checks I ran also passed.\n\n- **Validation:** each version must be exactly `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, using plain ASCII digits only. Leading zeros are rejected, except `0` itself. Pre-release tags, build metadata, extra spaces and a trailing newline all raise `ValueError`.\n- **Non-string input:** raises `TypeError`, as the README requires. This includes `None`, integers and bytes.\n- **Comparison:** the three parts are compared as whole numbers, so `1.10.0` counts as newer than `1.9.9`. The function returns `-1`, `0` or `1`.\n\nDONE: Rewrote `semver_compare` in solution.py to check the exact MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH format (ValueError for bad strings, TypeError for non-strings) and compare versions as number tuples; public tests pass.",
